1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:03,507
Lesson five is free
play: make your own game,

2
00:00:03,547 --> 00:00:04,687
with every block.

3
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:07,067
It starts with just
when the game starts.

4
00:00:07,267 --> 00:00:08,667
The rest is up to you.

5
00:00:08,967 --> 00:00:10,087
Stuck for ideas?

6
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:12,327
Show me the solution loads an example:

7
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:15,307
a ship that turns, flies,
and fires at rocks.

8
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:17,787
The ship turns and flies
with the arrow keys,

9
00:00:17,827 --> 00:00:19,907
and fires a shot with space.

10
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,127
Each shot flies forty steps,

11
00:00:22,227 --> 00:00:23,327
then deletes itself.

12
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:24,947
The rocks drift and bounce,

13
00:00:24,987 --> 00:00:27,407
and explode when a shot touches them.

14
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,240
Press Run, click the game, and fly.

15
00:00:30,633 --> 00:00:32,293
Hit all five rocks to win.

16
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:44,433
Every block has a tip: hold the
mouse over it to read what it does.

17
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:47,693
And Open in the playground takes
the DIV code of your blocks

18
00:00:47,733 --> 00:00:50,753
to the text editor,
to go on in real code.

19
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:52,240
That's all the lessons.

20
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,000
Have fun making your own games!
